{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "Aave",
  "name": "Aave ParaSwap repay and debt-swap adapters drained via leftover Augustus allowance",
  "summary": "The ParaSwap repay-with-collateral and debt-swap adapters' _buyOnParaSwap approved Augustus's TokenTransferProxy for the caller-declared maximum, ran caller-built Augustus calldata and never reset the allowance, so a swap that spent less left a live approval. Attackers used flash-loaned swapAndRepay/swapDebt calls with crafted calldata to spend those approvals on the token balances the adapters had accumulated, draining the V3 and V2 adapters on Ethereum, Arbitrum, Polygon, Optimism, Avalanche and BNB Chain.",
